%% user-build-route
%% Summary: Ground a task, choose a direct task, bounded goal or core pipeline, check the route can run here, then return advice and one ready-to-paste prompt.
%% Sources: skills/user-build-route/core.md
%% Not shown: the route criteria table, capacity and per-role support checks, bounded-goal prompt fields, deadline and blocker rules, and the exact output shape
%% Alt: A task is grounded in read-only evidence, given one of three routes, checked for conflicts or unknown capability on the host, and returned as advice with one ready-to-paste prompt; nothing is started.

flowchart TD
    A[Read the task, project instructions and plan] --> B{Task missing, or an answer would change the route?}
    B -- Yes, ask the operator --> A
    B -- No --> C[Weigh uncertainty, risk, scope and acceptance]
    C --> D{Which slice comes next?}
    D -- Direct task --> E[Contained, reversible, simple check]
    D -- Bounded goal --> F[Finite question with an observable finish line]
    D -- Core pipeline --> G[Delivery needs design, sequencing or review]
    E --> H{Route compatible with the task and host?}
    F --> H
    G --> H
    H -- Known conflict --> I[Name the conflict; offer the smallest supported route]
    H -- Unknown capability --> J[Make the prompt qualify first, stop on failure]
    H -- Compatible --> K[Prepare the route's next prompt with its gates]
    I --> K
    J --> K
    K --> L[Return Decision, Why, Next and one prompt; start nothing]
